  "summary": "A denial-of-service flood on ID 0x000, the highest-priority CAN ID, which is absent from the baseline. It was injected at 709.33 msg/s and accounts for 46% of all alert frames. Because bus capacity is fixed, legitimate traffic was displaced rather than augmented: total bus rate stayed below baseline (0.79x), all 26 baseline IDs ran below 70% of their expected rate, and 0x2B0 went completely silent. The constant all-zero payload and zero entropy confirm this is a flood, not a functional message.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The alert spans 0.50s to 5.75s (5.25s, 20 merged flagged windows) and contains 8091 frames from 27 arbitration IDs, with detector score 0.67.",
      "cites": ["E0"]
    },
    {
      "text": "0x000 is not in the baseline ID set and sent 3724 frames over the alert (709.33 msg/s) with payload entropy 0.000 bits.",
      "cites": ["E3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Frames from the baseline-absent ID 0x000 make up 3724 of the 8091 alert frames (46%).",
      "cites": ["E2", "E3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Average bus load over the alert was 1541 msg/s versus a 1953 msg/s baseline (0.79x), and even the busiest 0.5s window only reached 1.07x baseline, so total traffic did not increase despite the injection.",
      "cites": ["E1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Of 26 baseline IDs expected at a countable rate, all 26 ran below 70% of their baseline rate.",
      "cites": ["E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Individual known IDs 0x440, 0x370, 0x690, 0x260 and 0x5A0 each ran at only 0.44x to 0.57x of baseline with greatly stretched mean inter-frame gaps (e.g. 0x440 mean gap 22.785 ms vs 10.001 ms baseline).",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6", "E7", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "0x2B0 sent nothing during the alert although the baseline expects about 525 frames in that time.",
      "cites": ["E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sample frames show 0x000 carrying a constant all-zero 8-byte payload, consistent with a flood rather than legitimate data.",
      "cites": ["E10"]
    }
  ],
  "recommended_action": "Treat as an active bus flood. Identify and isolate the node injecting ID 0x000 (disconnect or silence it), or block/filter 0x000 at a gateway or intrusion-prevention point since it is absent from the baseline. After containment, verify that all suppressed IDs resume their baseline rates, in particular the fully silent 0x2B0, and investigate how the injecting node gained bus access."
}

